From aa0d68f034d176c4d352b99fb24b7e8d067db6b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:10:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: hdmi: Only ignore hotplug interrupts on forced
 connectors

vc4.force_hotplug is a per-connector bitmask, and detect only forces
the connectors whose bit is set. The hotplug interrupt handler instead
ignored interrupts on every connector whenever any bit was set.

As these connectors use DRM_CONNECTOR_POLL_HPD they are not polled, so
e.g. force_hotplug=2 (HDMI1 only) left HDMI0 status stuck after a plug
or unplug.

Check the connector's own bit, matching detect.

Fixes: cb7db28b9e17 ("vc4/hdmi: Ignore hotplug interrupt with force_hotplug")
Link: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7724
Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -2370,7 +2370,8 @@ static irqreturn_t vc4_hdmi_hpd_irq_thre
 	struct drm_connector *connector = &vc4_hdmi->connector;
 	struct drm_device *dev = connector->dev;
 
-	if (dev && dev->registered && !force_hotplug)
+	if (dev && dev->registered &&
+	    !(force_hotplug & BIT(vc4_hdmi->encoder.type - VC4_ENCODER_TYPE_HDMI0)))
 		drm_connector_helper_hpd_irq_event(connector);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
